{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-001", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "paired ovaries", "grades": [5], "en": "A girl has two ovaries, which are small oval organs that make egg cells and sit one on each side of the uterus.", "terms": ["ovaries", "obaryo", "ovaryo", "egg cells", "itlog", "uterus", "matris", "mga obaryo"], "source": "DepEd G5 Science; encyclopedia-stable anatomy", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 1, "dedup_nearest": "dcard:dcard-08970", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.7742, "sha": "82c76bb20766e646", "id": "paired-ovaries-g5"}
{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-002", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "ovary releases eggs", "grades": [5], "en": "Each ovary stores tiny egg cells, and one job of an ovary is to release an egg cell when the body is ready.", "terms": ["ovary", "obaryo", "egg cell", "itlog", "release", "naglalabas", "gipagawas", "selula"], "source": "encyclopedia-stable; NRC LS1.B", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 2, "dedup_nearest": "bees-queen-lays-eggs-g4", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.8008, "sha": "9cb840d1565483d7", "id": "ovary-releases-eggs-g5"}
{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-003", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "ovaries on diagrams", "grades": [5], "en": "In a labeled diagram of the female body, the ovaries are the two oval parts drawn beside the uterus.", "terms": ["labeled diagram", "ovaries", "obaryo", "larawan", "hulagway", "dayagram", "uterus", "matris"], "source": "DepEd G5 Science; textbook anatomy diagrams", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 3, "dedup_nearest": "dcard:dcard-08970", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.7674, "sha": "e74844a910bb11d6", "id": "ovaries-on-diagrams-g5"}
{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-004", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "ovary hormones", "grades": [5], "en": "Ovaries also make chemical messengers called hormones that help a girl's reproductive organs grow and work.", "terms": ["ovaries", "hormones", "obaryo", "hormon", "reproductive", "pagpaparami", "pagpanganak", "babaye"], "source": "encyclopedia-stable; NRC LS1.A", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 4, "dedup_nearest": "dcard:dcard-02487", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.8169, "sha": "ee2bb74a718aa3ab", "id": "ovary-hormones-g5"}
{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-005", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "ovary size location", "grades": [5], "en": "An ovary is about the size of a large almond and lies deep in the lower belly, not on the outside of the body.", "terms": ["ovary", "obaryo", "size", "laki", "gidak-on", "belly", "tiyan", "almond"], "source": "encyclopedia-stable anatomy (ovary size comparison)", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 5, "dedup_nearest": "dcard:dcard-02410", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.7675, "sha": "05a5e7717080cc8b", "id": "ovary-size-location-g5"}
{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-006", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "egg cells stored", "grades": [5], "en": "A girl is born with egg cells already stored in her ovaries, and those ovaries keep the egg cells safe.", "terms": ["egg cells", "itlog", "ovaries", "obaryo", "stored", "nakatago", "gitipig", "born"], "source": "encyclopedia-stable; NRC LS1.B", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 6, "dedup_nearest": "weaverbird-eggs-inside-g5", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.7889, "sha": "42da6dca460b9ee6", "id": "egg-cells-stored-g5"}
{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-007", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "ovary label lines", "grades": [5], "en": "On many textbook pictures, a line labeled ovary points to a small oval organ to the left or right of the uterus.", "terms": ["label", "ovary", "obaryo", "larawan", "timaan", "dayagram", "uterus", "matris"], "source": "DepEd G5 Science; labeled-diagram practice", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 7, "dedup_nearest": "nectar-guides-point-to-nectar-g7", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.678, "sha": "37b9ef03ffb3a8c7", "id": "ovary-label-lines-g5"}
{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-008", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "ovaries work in pairs", "grades": [5], "en": "The two ovaries work as a pair, so the female reproductive system has one ovary on each side.", "terms": ["two ovaries", "obaryo", "pair", "magkapares", "magkauban", "female", "babae", "babaye"], "source": "encyclopedia-stable anatomy", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 8, "dedup_nearest": "dcard:dcard-11033", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.724, "sha": "122477d079b43011", "id": "ovaries-work-in-pairs-g5"}
{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-009", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "egg travels toward uterus", "grades": [5], "en": "After an ovary releases an egg cell, that egg cell can travel toward the uterus along a connecting tube.", "terms": ["egg cell", "itlog", "ovary", "obaryo", "uterus", "matris", "tagoangkan", "tube"], "source": "encyclopedia-stable; NRC LS1.B", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 9, "dedup_nearest": "pollen-tube-fertilization-g7", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.8328, "sha": "ec445a6ef013ec37", "id": "egg-travels-toward-uterus-g5"}
{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-010", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "ovaries are internal", "grades": [5], "en": "Ovaries are internal organs, so you cannot see them from the outside the way you can see skin or hair.", "terms": ["internal", "ovaries", "obaryo", "sa loob", "sulod", "organs", "organo", "hidden"], "source": "encyclopedia-stable anatomy", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 10, "dedup_nearest": "ffct:ffct-02628", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.7245, "sha": "570f083aec5a35ea", "id": "ovaries-are-internal-g5"}
{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-011", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "uterus holds baby", "grades": [5], "en": "The uterus is a hollow, muscular organ in the lower belly that can hold and protect a growing baby.", "terms": ["uterus", "matris", "sinapupunan", "tagoangkan", "bahay-bata", "womb", "baby", "sanggol"], "source": "DepEd G5 Science; encyclopedia-stable anatomy", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 11, "dedup_nearest": "dcard:dcard-01072", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.8307, "sha": "e18fd271c9161676", "id": "uterus-holds-baby-g5"}
{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-012", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "pear-shaped uterus", "grades": [5], "en": "In labeled diagrams, the uterus is the pear-shaped organ in the center, with an ovary on each side.", "terms": ["uterus", "matris", "pear-shaped", "dayagram", "larawan", "ovary", "obaryo", "hulagway"], "source": "textbook anatomy diagrams; encyclopedia-stable", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 12, "dedup_nearest": "cnidarian-radial-symmetry-g7", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.7798, "sha": "3af6b9c5089b81df", "id": "pear-shaped-uterus-g5"}
{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-013", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "uterus walls stretch", "grades": [5], "en": "The thick muscle walls of the uterus can stretch slowly so there is room if a baby is growing inside.", "terms": ["uterus", "matris", "muscle", "kalamnan", "kaunuran", "stretch", "lumalawak", "motuy-od"], "source": "encyclopedia-stable anatomy", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 13, "dedup_nearest": "barnacle-hard-grows-as-animal-grows-g6", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.771, "sha": "1b52e765e99b1a2a", "id": "uterus-walls-stretch-g5"}
{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-014", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "uterus in pelvis", "grades": [5], "en": "The uterus sits in the pelvis, the bowl of bone at the bottom of the trunk, behind the bladder.", "terms": ["uterus", "matris", "pelvis", "balakang", "pantog", "bladder", "tagoangkan", "buto"], "source": "encyclopedia-stable anatomy", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 14, "dedup_nearest": "ffct:ffct-11225", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.8444, "sha": "03925f041f503101", "id": "uterus-in-pelvis-g5"}
{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-015", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "bladder is not reproductive", "grades": [5], "en": "The bladder stores urine, so on a pelvic diagram do not label it as the uterus or as the prostate.", "terms": ["bladder", "pantog", "uterus", "matris", "prostate", "ihi", "diagram", "dayagram"], "source": "DepEd G5 Science; labeled-diagram practice", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 15, "dedup_nearest": "marsupial-young-finishes-growing-outside-womb-g5", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.7263, "sha": "9a3db48b5518c91c", "id": "bladder-is-not-reproductive-g5"}
{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-016", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "uterus inner lining", "grades": [5], "en": "The inner lining of the uterus is a soft cushion that can support a tiny developing baby.", "terms": ["uterus", "matris", "lining", "sapin", "sulod", "baby", "sanggol", "sinapupunan"], "source": "encyclopedia-stable anatomy", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 16, "dedup_nearest": "dcard:dcard-08330", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.8215, "sha": "bf8c01717569097e", "id": "uterus-inner-lining-g5"}
{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-017", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "uterus joins vagina", "grades": [5], "en": "The uterus is connected at the bottom to the vagina, so the two organs form one continuous pathway.", "terms": ["uterus", "matris", "vagina", "daanan", "pathway", "dalan", "tagoangkan", "connected"], "source": "encyclopedia-stable anatomy", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 17, "dedup_nearest": "dcard:dcard-11036", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.701, "sha": "16b614190bb0e08f", "id": "uterus-joins-vagina-g5"}
{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-018", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "uterus also called womb", "grades": [5], "en": "Another everyday name for the uterus is the womb, and both words mean the same pear-shaped organ.", "terms": ["uterus", "womb", "matris", "sinapupunan", "bahay-bata", "tagoangkan", "pear-shaped", "organo"], "source": "encyclopedia-stable; DepEd G5 Science", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 18, "dedup_nearest": "ffct:ffct-11316", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.7531, "sha": "33df5f262588182a", "id": "uterus-also-called-womb-g5"}
{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-019", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "one uterus only", "grades": [5], "en": "Unlike the paired ovaries, there is only one uterus in the female reproductive system of a person.", "terms": ["uterus", "matris", "one", "isa", "usa", "ovaries", "obaryo", "female"], "source": "encyclopedia-stable anatomy", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 19, "dedup_nearest": "dcard:dcard-00163", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.6953, "sha": "d79eef43940e4a71", "id": "one-uterus-only-g5"}
{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-020", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "uterus side-view diagram", "grades": [5], "en": "On a side-view diagram, the uterus appears as a thick-walled pouch sitting behind the bladder in the pelvis.", "terms": ["side-view", "uterus", "matris", "bladder", "pantog", "dayagram", "backbone", "gulugod"], "source": "textbook sagittal diagrams; encyclopedia-stable", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 20, "dedup_nearest": "platypus-venom-spur-size-example-g6", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.7685, "sha": "a2c035dfa8b7c0be", "id": "uterus-side-view-diagram-g5"}
{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-021", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "vagina connecting tube", "grades": [5], "en": "The vagina is a muscular tube that connects the uterus to the outside of the body.", "terms": ["vagina", "uterus", "matris", "tube", "daanan", "dalan", "muscular", "kalamnan"], "source": "DepEd G5 Science; encyclopedia-stable anatomy", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 21, "dedup_nearest": "dcard:dcard-01073", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.7814, "sha": "0580ceaa81802339", "id": "vagina-connecting-tube-g5"}
