{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-023", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "vagina stretchy walls", "grades": [5], "en": "The walls of the vagina are stretchy and muscular, so the tube can change shape as the body needs.", "terms": ["vagina", "stretchy", "lumalawak", "motuy-od", "muscular", "daanan", "walls", "dingding"], "source": "encyclopedia-stable anatomy", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 23, "dedup_nearest": "stomach-muscles-squeeze-make-sound-g4", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.7758, "sha": "61b70f0867fd9261", "id": "vagina-stretchy-walls-g5"}
{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-025", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "ovary hormones reach uterus", "grades": [5], "en": "Hormones made in the ovaries travel in the blood and can reach the uterus to help it do its job.", "terms": ["hormones", "ovaries", "obaryo", "uterus", "matris", "dugo", "blood", "hormon"], "source": "encyclopedia-stable; NRC LS1.A", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 25, "dedup_nearest": "ffct:ffct-09299", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.8122, "sha": "8a686f5294200f6b", "id": "ovary-hormones-reach-uterus-g5"}
{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-026", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "vagina label line", "grades": [5], "en": "A label line that points to the canal under the uterus on a female diagram is usually naming the vagina.", "terms": ["label", "vagina", "uterus", "matris", "diagram", "dayagram", "timaan", "daanan"], "source": "DepEd G5 Science; labeled-diagram practice", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 26, "dedup_nearest": "dcard:dcard-00969", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.6989, "sha": "05ad3f74b51769e8", "id": "vagina-label-line-g5"}
{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-027", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "vagina last pathway", "grades": [5], "en": "The vagina leads from the uterus to the outside, so it is the last part of the female reproductive pathway.", "terms": ["vagina", "uterus", "matris", "pathway", "dalan", "daanan", "female", "babaye"], "source": "encyclopedia-stable anatomy", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 27, "dedup_nearest": "dcard:dcard-01074", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.7478, "sha": "cd12561374bbc016", "id": "vagina-last-pathway-g5"}
{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-028", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "vagina narrower than uterus", "grades": [5], "en": "Compared with the pear-shaped uterus above it, the vagina looks like a narrower tube on most diagrams.", "terms": ["vagina", "uterus", "matris", "diagram", "dayagram", "tube", "daanan", "larawan"], "source": "textbook anatomy diagrams", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 28, "dedup_nearest": "tamaraw-v-shaped-horns-g5", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.7614, "sha": "3f31f52d0578559a", "id": "vagina-narrower-than-uterus-g5"}
{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-029", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "uterus and vagina muscle", "grades": [5], "en": "Both the uterus and the vagina have muscular walls, so they can squeeze and change shape when they work.", "terms": ["uterus", "matris", "vagina", "muscular", "kalamnan", "kaunuran", "squeeze", "pumisil"], "source": "encyclopedia-stable anatomy", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 29, "dedup_nearest": "stomach-muscles-squeeze-make-sound-g4", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.8246, "sha": "58c36a3f35758bdf", "id": "uterus-and-vagina-muscle-g5"}
{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-030", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "finding the vagina", "grades": [5], "en": "You identify the vagina on a picture by finding the tube that links the uterus to the outside of the body.", "terms": ["identify", "vagina", "picture", "larawan", "hulagway", "uterus", "matris", "tube"], "source": "DepEd G5 Science; picture identification", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 30, "dedup_nearest": "urethra-urine-exit-g7", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.7207, "sha": "724d9b5299bf3a83", "id": "finding-the-vagina-g5"}
{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-031", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "paired testes make sperm", "grades": [5], "en": "A boy has two testes, which are oval organs that make sperm, the male sex cells.", "terms": ["testes", "testis", "sperm", "lalaki", "sex cells", "selula", "oval", "testicle"], "source": "DepEd G5 Science; encyclopedia-stable anatomy", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 31, "dedup_nearest": "dcard:dcard-12480", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.8547, "sha": "f5d6032edfd3e17a", "id": "paired-testes-make-sperm-g5"}
{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-032", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "testes in skin pouch", "grades": [5], "en": "Each testis hangs in a small pouch of skin outside the main body, where the temperature stays a little cooler.", "terms": ["testis", "testes", "pouch", "supot", "panit", "skin", "cooler", "malamig"], "source": "encyclopedia-stable anatomy", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 32, "dedup_nearest": "dcard:dcard-12495", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.8381, "sha": "0e22b309e3a80db3", "id": "testes-in-skin-pouch-g5"}
{"tmp_id": "lane-a-G5-L-3-033", "brief_code": "G5-L-3", "domain": "LIVING_THINGS", "topic": "why testes sit outside", "grades": [5], "en": "Sperm need a slightly cooler place than inside the belly, which is one reason the testes sit outside the body.", "terms": ["sperm", "testes", "cooler", "tiyan", "belly", "temperature", "temperatura", "gawas"], "source": "encyclopedia-stable; sperm production temperature", "card_form": "fact", "confidence": 3, "_stream": "G5-L-3", "_line": 33, "dedup_nearest": "ffct:ffct-13382", "dedup_cos_bank": 0.8028, "sha": "fa7a6e906db6407a", "id": "why-testes-sit-outside-g5"}
